<title>UK: UK's Labour announces tax-cutting manifesto.</title>
<headline>UK's Labour announces tax-cutting manifesto.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tony Blair, leader of the opposition labour Party tipped to win Britain's May 1 election, said on Wednesday the party had agreed a manifesto which he said &quot;marks the burial of tax-and-spend policitcs from Labour&quot;.</p>
<p>The key policies in the manifesto include a pledge not to increase income tax rates for the full five years of a Labour government, a promise to cut VAT (Value Added Tax) on heating to five percent and an &quot;ambition&quot; to cut the starting rate of income tax to 10 percent.</p>
</text>
